### Withdrawal API Tests
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/withdraw

### 0. Upload the payout QR image (multipart, field name: qrCodeImage)
POST {{baseUrl}}/qr
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="qrCodeImage"; filename="payout-qr.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./payout-qr.png
------boundary--

### 1. Create Withdrawal (amount in INR, UPI id, optional QR url from step 0)
POST {{baseUrl}}/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "81acb703-4f9c-49b2-ad67-50505bbe7338",
  "amount": 500.00,
  "upiId": "member@bank",
  "qrCodeUrl": "http://localhost:4000/uploads/payout-qr/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000.png"
}

### 2. Get All Withdrawals
GET {{baseUrl}}/all

### 3. Get Withdrawal by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 4. Update Withdrawal
PUT {{baseUrl}}/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 750.00,
  "status": "APPROVED"
}

### 5. Delete Withdrawal
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 6. Get Withdrawals by User ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/a0cdf2dc-1af2-436b-bd0f-c3461599b3f6
